(2135, 'recognition', 1, '/ˌrek.əɡˈnɪʃ.ən/', '(biology) the ability of one molecule to attach to another molecule that has a complementary shape', '\"molecular recognition drives all of biology, for instance, hormone and receptor or antibody-antigen interactions or the organization of molecules into larger biologically active entities\"'),
