(13787, 'bottle', 1, '/ˈbɒtəl/', 'a glass or plastic vessel used for storing drinks or other liquids; typically cylindrical without handles and with a narrow neck that can be plugged or capped', '\"He opened a bottle of water after the long hike.\"'),
(13788, 'bottle', 1, '/ˈbɒtəl/', 'a vessel fitted with a flexible teat and filled with milk or formula; used as a substitute for breast feeding infants and very young children', '\"The baby drank her milk from a bottle.\"'),
