(51998, 'profound', 3, '/prəˈfaʊnd/', 'situated at or extending to great depth; too deep to have been sounded or plumbed; \"the dark unfathomed caves of ocean\"-Thomas Gray', '\"the profound depths of the sea\"; \"unplumbed depths of the sea\"; \"remote and unsounded caverns\"'),
